:: Widgets DoLX Changelog [widget]
<<widget "DoLXChangelog">>
	<div class="changelog-overlay">
		<div class="changelog-hero">
			<span class="changelog-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128220;</span>
			<div>
				<div class="changelog-label">PATCH NOTES</div>
				<h1>DoL X-Change <span>v0.22.1</span></h1>
				<div class="changelog-apk-note"><strong>Official X-Change APK:</strong> Join the DoL Modding server and check the dedicated <a href="https://discord.com/channels/675158131688603721/1512272787572785162" target="_blank">X-Change Channel</a>.</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		<a class="changelog-release-link" href="https://gitgud.io/Akoz/dol-xchange/-/releases" target="_blank"><span aria-hidden="true">&#128279;</span> View the full changelog and all releases <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span></a>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon new" aria-hidden="true">&#10022;</span> Changes and Additions</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Update the credits list for better clarity and consistency</strong>.
		</li>
		</ul>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Tidy up some menus, UIs, and codes</strong>.
		</li>
		</ul>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Added Seaspray Hotel on Mer Street</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added a run-down hotel where players with enough Housekeeping can ask the front desk for cleaning work.</li>
		<li>Guest rooms include different jobs: messy rooms, difficult guests, and corridor encounters.</li>
		<li>At night, rooms can be broken into for cash, jewellery, and safes, with one room able to trigger a police call.</li>
		<li>Room 112 can eventually become a rentable room after cleaning it and reporting back to the front desk.</li>
		<li>Rent starts at <strong>£100 per week</strong> and can increase depending on usage.</li>
		<li>The room provides a good bed away from Bailey, a bathroom, mirror, and somewhere to bring guests charmed in the hotel lobby.</li>
		<li>Missing three weeks of rent causes the hotel to reclaim the key.</li>
		<li>Heavy hotel usage can eventually trigger a manager interaction about what they have seen on the cameras.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Bank can now pay Seaspray Hotel rent</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Room 112 rent can be set up as an HBSC standing order, similar to Bailey's rent.</li>
		<li>Rent is automatically taken from savings when due.</li>
		<li>If savings cannot cover the payment, the standing order is cancelled.</li>
		<li>The front desk can also take payment directly from savings.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Cat transformation</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>Keen Ears</strong>, allowing Cat characters to recognise stalkers by their footsteps before they reach the player.</li>
		<li>Fully feline characters are harder to catch when someone pounces on them.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Swat</strong> to bat away a tentacle with claws, including during consensual scenes.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Chirrup</strong> for greeting dogs, wolves, and foxes instead of hissing.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Slink</strong> and <strong>Preen</strong> Attitude options.</li>
		<li>Cats can hiss two farm dogs apart instead of scolding them.</li>
		<li>Cats can nap during any lesson even when fully rested.</li>
		<li>Added an option to bat at Harper's pen instead of entering hypnosis.</li>
		<li>Cat characters rest better around midday and late at night, but worse around dawn and dusk.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Kasha</strong> transformation: Cat + Demon.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Cat Sith</strong> transformation: Cat + Fallen Angel.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Fortune Stealing</strong> for Kasha, allowing one luck-stealing attempt per encounter with enough Skulduggery.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Ill Omen</strong> for Cat Sith, reducing an attacker's accuracy for the rest of the fight if the player's Willpower suffecient.</li>
		<li>Cat Sith gains new ear and tail art with separately recolourable markings by <strong>FoxIsASalmon!?</strong></li>
		<li>Added new Cat scenes with Bailey and Avery.</li>
		<li>Story by <strong>Cappy (@cannymeows)</strong> and <strong>D.N.A.</strong></li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added new flower seeds</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>Daffodil</strong>, <strong>Hibiscus</strong>, <strong>Pansy</strong>, and <strong>Primrose</strong>.</li>
		<li>Seeds can be found while exploring the island or around the Water Dragon nest.</li>
		<li>Finding flower seeds also grants a matching flower hairpin.</li>
		<li>If the player's head is bare, the hairpin is worn automatically; otherwise it is sent to the wardrobe.</li>
		<li>Lily, Tulip, and Sunflower seeds now follow the same hairpin behaviour.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a new Ear Slime command</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Ear Slimes can now order the player to <strong>take one of your gray X-Change pills</strong>.</li>
		<li>Requires sleeping at home and at least 50 Ear Slime Corruption.</li>
		<li>Only appears when a usable Gray pill is actually available.</li>
		<li>The Ear Slime may prefer certain pills depending on its current focus, such as pregnancy or impregnation.</li>
		<li><strong>Obey</strong> takes the pill immediately before returning to bed.</li>
		<li><strong>Defy</strong> and <strong>Ignore</strong> work like other Ear Slime tasks.</li>
		<li>Gray Agent currently treats <strong>Obey</strong> as willingly taking the pill, so Gray-pill gender swapping is not blocked.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Silver Reversal pill</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The Silver Stranger at the docks can now cure permanent X-Change transformations.</li>
		<li>A one-time <strong>Silver Reversal</strong> pill can be purchased for <strong>£150,000</strong>.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added X-Change pill tracking to Extra Stats</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Extra Stats now shows how many X-Change pills the player has taken.</li>
		<li>It also tracks how many times the player has been spiked.</li>
		<li>Existing saves cannot recover past spike counts, so the <strong>spiked</strong> counter starts from 0.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added market stall upgrades</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>After the first sale, the market office on Connudatus Street can upgrade the player's stall.</li>
		<li><strong>Looks</strong> upgrades attract more customers and help with expensive goods or overcharging.</li>
		<li><strong>Safety</strong> upgrades slow customer Arousal and reduce lewd incidents.</li>
		<li><strong>Profit</strong> upgrades increase income from certain goods, with a glass showcase boosting all sales.</li>
		<li><strong>Bags</strong> upgrades can make customers buy more, and regulars may bring their own bags.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Oral Fixation</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added the <strong>Oral Fixation</strong> trait, earned through giving oral and swallowing cum.</li>
		<li>Unlocks the <strong>Throat Goat</strong> feat.</li>
		<li>Makes the mouth much more sensitive and normally requires oral stimulation to orgasm.</li>
		<li>Swallowed cum can optionally allow normal orgasm for the next hour.</li>
		<li>Swallowing cum also builds Nectar addiction and gives the same aphrodisiac/dizzy effects as plant nectar.</li>
		<li>If a scene provides no way to satisfy the trait, staying edged too long eventually causes a hollow, stressful orgasm instead of leaving the player stuck.</li>
		<li>Can be disabled under <strong>Settings &gt; Traits</strong>.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded orgasm restriction settings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Breeder, Omega, Alpha, Cock/Hole Addict, and Oral Fixation</strong> now each have their own <strong>Allow orgasm</strong> option.</li>
		<li>When enabled, orgasm is possible without satisfying the trait, but feels hollow and causes Stress.</li>
		<li>More scenes now respect the individual restriction options.</li>
		<li>Orgasm restrictions are temporarily disabled during <strong>Gwylan's ritual</strong> so the event can always progress.</li>
		<li>During <strong>Hopeless Cycle</strong>, X-Change effects tied to the altered state are temporarily paused and restored afterwards, including orgasm restrictions, Alpha/Omega effects, pheromones, Heat/Rut, and Chastity/Arousal Acclimated.</li>
		<li>Clarified several pill-setting descriptions.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added NPC multi-orgasm chance setting</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>Settings &gt; NPC Multi-Orgasm</strong> with a default generic NPC chance of 20%.</li>
		<li>Generic NPCs now use the same base chance instead of varying heavily by sex and level.</li>
		<li>NPCs that trigger it orgasm at least twice, with higher-level NPCs able to go more times.</li>
		<li>The men/women filter still works.</li>
		<li>Named NPCs and beasts are unchanged.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added Clear Climax fetish setting</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Clear Climax</strong> under Penis-related gameplay settings, disabled by default.</li>
		<li>Very low semen can temporarily cause orgasms to produce thin, clear fluid instead of normal cum.</li>
		<li>The player cannot impregnate anyone while in this state.</li>
		<li>Added <strong>Clear Climax</strong> insecurity.</li>
		<li>Normal semen returns after sufficient recovery.</li>
		<li>The insecurity fades gradually and can be overcome through at the lake or temple.</li>
		<li>Fully accepting it unlocks <strong>Acceptance: Clear Climax</strong>.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added new background trait: Detached</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Available during Character Creation under Mental Attributes.</li>
		<li>Stress builds 35% slower, though Pain still causes normal Stress and reduces the benefit as injury increases.</li>
		<li>Named-character Love grows 25% slower but also falls 20% slower.</li>
		<li>The player's face stays calm instead of blushing or showing Arousal.</li>
		<li>Pain still shows, while orgasm or very high Stress can break through the calm expression.</li>
		<li>Some characters notice that the player is difficult to read.</li>
		<li>Arousal, Pain, Trauma, and Lust otherwise behave normally.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added demon essence from non-penetrative sex</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Demons at transformation level 6+ can absorb sexual essence by tasting a partner's fluids or through tribbing.</li>
		<li>This can trigger the usual Trauma relief and Willpower recovery once per encounter.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Great Hawk access and added Prey clothing trait</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gwylan can teach a hawk call after the player asks about strengthening their wings.</li>
		<li>The call can be used once per day deeper in the moor to make the Great Hawk appear.</li>
		<li>Added the <strong>Prey</strong> clothing trait.</li>
		<li>Prey clothing makes wolves, boars, and bears in the forest and the Great Hawk on the moor more likely to find the player.</li>
		<li>Can be disabled under <strong>Settings &gt; Modded Clothing Traits</strong>.</li>
		<li><strong>Realistic Clothing Transparency</strong> is now located in the same settings group.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added a music player to POCKET</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Buy headphones from the Furniture Shop's <strong>Electronics</strong> catalogue to unlock the <strong>Music</strong> tab.</li>
		<li>Listen to the game soundtrack or add custom music.</li>
		<li>Includes play/pause, skip, stop, repeat, seeking, search, favourites, and song reordering.</li>
		<li>Playlist presets preserve custom songs, order, and favourites.</li>
		<li>Removing headphones pauses playback and resumes from the same point when worn again.</li>
		<li>Headphones are available in 12 colours.</li>
		<li>Art by <strong>nicos</strong> for the vanilla sprite.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Headphones now help autistic characters in loud places</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Headphones reduce sensory Load and Stress from noisy areas.</li>
		<li>Playing music increases the effect.</li>
		<li>Headphones also reduce awareness of sounds, disabling Sharp Hearing and making it easier for people to approach unnoticed outdoors.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Added maggot toggle</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>Enable maggots</strong> under Creature Settings, enabled by default.</li>
		<li>Turning it off removes maggots from landfill and brothel events and prevents normal maggot parasite pregnancies.</li>
		<li>Debug and cheat options are unaffected.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Tweaks and Rebalancing</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed demon purple skin getting stuck after using X-Change</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Skin colour now returns to normal after swapping back if the demon transformation is no longer active.</li>
		<li>Existing affected saves should also fix themselves after reloading.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed custom makeup colours</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Skip desaturate filter</strong> is now enabled by default.</li>
		<li>Older saves enable it once automatically so custom blusher no longer renders black.</li>
		<li>Toggling the option updates the preview immediately.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved the character creation randomiser</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Random appearance now updates the preview after genital changes.</li>
		<li>Random hair colour and length now use the full available selection, including unique colours, Ebony, and all six lengths.</li>
		<li>Random breast, ass, penis, and body sizes use their full ranges again, including Tall/Giant bodies and sizes above Pert.</li>
		<li>Random demeanour includes modded demeanours.</li>
		<li>Fully random starts respect the character's growth limits.</li>
		<li>Fixed skin tone/shade choices resetting to Neutral/Light after menu refreshes.</li>
		<li>This also fixes X-Change sexflipped skin options.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated clothing sets</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Old sets created before the Bag slot existed now treat Bag as empty, removing the current bag instead of leaving it equipped.</li>
		<li>Sets that already contain a bag continue to work normally.</li>
		<li>Scarves are now saved and restored properly.</li>
		<li>If a set has no saved colour for an item, the currently worn colour is kept.</li>
		<li>Fixed the set editor replacing the main item colour with the accessory colour.</li>
		<li>Imported sets now correctly update scarves, earrings, and rings.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated wardrobe selection behaviour</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Scarves and bags no longer randomly swap after changing another clothing slot or equipping a set.</li>
		<li>The wardrobe now clears each slot's selection after equipping it.</li>
		<li>This should also prevent the same issue with future clothing slots.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded ambience</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Indoor ambience is more lightly muffled.</li>
		<li>Added a coin sound when buying items.</li>
		<li>Added a medication-click sound when taking medicine.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Avery rent support</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Talking to Avery or serving a meal now counts as showing up.</li>
		<li>Every meal served clears one missed dinner.</li>
		<li>Avery can still comment on a long absence the first time the player returns.</li>
		<li>Fixed the Journal saying Avery was still covering rent after they stopped.</li>
		<li>Avery now tells the player when rent support ends after their fall.</li>
		<li>Bailey's night visits are restored after Avery kicks the player out.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Expanded Underground Hunt</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Added <strong>Let them catch you</strong> during consensual/paid brothel runs.</li>
		<li>Skips the Athletics escape roll and sends the player directly to the existing caught outcome.</li>
		<li>Prevents accidental contract failure from escaping.</li>
		<li>Only appears with the Underground brothel contract.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Buffed Harpy transformation</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The Harpy income bonus now applies to all Housekeeping jobs, including office, pound, chalets, hotel, flats, and house calls.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Robin's rent</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Robin's rent now scales with Bailey's, including rent settings and economy inflation.</li>
		<li>Robin can fall behind if their income cannot cover rent.</li>
		<li>Unpaid rent becomes debt and is taken from future income first.</li>
		<li>After five weeks of growing debt, the player starts paying for Robin again.</li>
		<li>Robin only takes over rent when the stand earns enough to cover the current amount.</li>
		<li>Robin can regain independence later if circumstances improve.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Robin's Give Money screen</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Shows Robin's current savings.</li>
		<li>Shows how much Bailey takes each week.</li>
		<li>Shows how many weeks behind Robin is on payments.</li>
		<li>The overdue warning appears only after at least one missed week.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Sex pain now depends more on skill, Arousal, and consent</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Higher skill reduces Pain.</li>
		<li>Arousal reduces Pain during consensual sex.</li>
		<li>Forced oral is more painful than consensual oral.</li>
		<li>Continuous oral gradually causes jaw strain and tiredness.</li>
		<li>Oral skill reduces the strain.</li>
		<li>Jaw strain resets when the mouth is free.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Whitney Wild Night</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Repeat night visits can randomly use either the Wild or Emotional route.</li>
		<li>The chance is influenced by Whitney's Dominance.</li>
		<li>At Dominance 70, the chance is 70% Wild and 30% Emotional.</li>
		<li>The original route choice remains stored for other events.</li>
		<li>At maximum Love, Whitney now visits every week instead of sometimes skipping a week.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated hallway events</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Lockpicking another student out of a locker without asking for money now grants <strong>+Status</strong>.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
		<h2><span class="changelog-section-icon fixes" aria-hidden="true">&#9874;</span> Fixes and Improvements</h2>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Fixed Office Executive assignments</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Coats and jackets no longer cause errors with topless/bottomless clothing requests.</li>
		<li>Shoe requests now reference and sell the correct shoes at the correct price.</li>
		<li>Foot-related content respects the Foot Fetish setting.</li>
		<li>Clothes removed for the executive are returned if the file-stealing fight interrupts the scene.</li>
		<li>Giving up during the fight no longer leads to a blank page.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Restored Adult Shop clothing</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Restored the muzzle, gag, doggy muzzle, wood muzzle, small sailor's hat, sailor shorts, and short sailor shirt.</li>
		<li>Fixed the short sailor shirt's fishing-shop tag.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Hairdresser scenes with Sydney</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Changing options while Sydney is present no longer crashes or errors.</li>
		<li>Sydney's seat uses the correct options from the start.</li>
		<li>Hair preview falls back correctly to the player's current colour.</li>
		<li>Unknown and modded colours no longer break the preview.</li>
		<li>Special/modded two-tone dyes no longer take money without applying the dye.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed World Override anatomy</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Black Wolf, Great Hawk, and Night Monster now preserve their selected anatomy, including encounter copies.</li>
		<li>Presentation gender still follows the chosen World Override.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed collars and scarves</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed police shock collars, prison intake, Eden, beach abduction, Underground scenes, chalets, Gwylan rituals, brothel contracts, and leash interactions.</li>
		<li>Collars remain the correct collar when attaching or removing a leash.</li>
		<li>Scarves display correctly in combat and can appear as random clothing rewards.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Migrated clothing lookup to names</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Clothing is now looked up by name instead of internal-list position.</li>
		<li>Prevents scenes from giving or checking the wrong clothing after list reordering.</li>
		<li>Fixed the hairdresser mirror dressing the player in a removed kaiju costume.</li>
		<li>Fixed the market-stall Ear Slime checking the wrong clothing for gingham/checkered items.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed sex acts incorrectly changing Gender Identity</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Partner orgasms, losing virginity, creampies, and breast play no longer affect the Gender Identity meter.</li>
		<li>Gender Identity changes from non-sexual sources, such as clothing and events, are unchanged.</li>
		<li>The player's own orgasms can still cause Dysphoria or comfort depending on the genitals involved, but no longer shift Gender Identity.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey's Autism rent event</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>The event no longer triggers during normal Sunday rent collection.</li>
		<li>The late-rent explanation option now appears only when rent is actually overdue.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pet interaction scenes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Pet slimes now actually feed on the player and can reach a proper scene ending.</li>
		<li>The player strips as described.</li>
		<li>Fighting the slime off still leaves it hungry.</li>
		<li>Chastity belts make the slime give up immediately.</li>
		<li>Fixed the snake's <strong>let it wander over you</strong> scene in the same way.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bird Tower feather dusters</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Crafting a feather duster no longer gives a walking cane.</li>
		<li>Building the wardrobe no longer replaces a hanging duster with a cane.</li>
		<li>The tower checks the correct wardrobe for stored dusters.</li>
		<li>A second duster cannot be crafted while one is already hanging.</li>
		<li>Crafting a feather duster or feathered hair clip now grants Housekeeping practice.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Reduced long-session lag, again</strong>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Avery body-part dialogue</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fingering and virginity lines now match the body part Avery is actually touching.</li>
		<li>Avery only learns virginity when the relevant dialogue actually occurs.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed masochism gain from Pain</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Climaxing while in Pain now raises Masochism properly.</li>
		<li>At 100+ Masochism, Pain once again gives strong Arousal.</li>
		<li>Below 100, Pain remains a turn-off as intended.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Gwylan pumpkin outfit and Scarf storage</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gwylan's pumpkin outfit conversation works even with fewer than five known recipes.</li>
		<li>Newly created storage locations now correctly include a Scarf compartment.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed labour after Harper's lab</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Harper's unfertilised egg-laying scene no longer incorrectly marks a separate baby pregnancy as already giving birth.</li>
		<li>Affected saves repair automatically on load.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pirate travel and Gwylan reunion</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Gwylan's reunion no longer breaks the forest shop after a long absence without captivity.</li>
		<li>Gwylan only references captivity since the player's last visit.</li>
		<li>Water Dragon Lab captivity is recognised correctly.</li>
		<li>Repeat prison sentences are no longer described as the first.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed chastity key holder</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Bailey is correctly named as the chastity-key holder after the orphanage fight and keeps the key.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Wren DoLP's voyeurism story</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Wren's card scene now uses the correct pronouns after references to the lady.</li>
		<li>Pronouns are also correct during the face-wiping line.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Improved Lockpicking failure feedback</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Failed checks now explain when Skulduggery is being reduced by transformations or other effects, even if the visible stat meets the requirement.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Museum painting scenes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Bleeding Ward no longer errors when Winter's pregnancy cannot happen.</li>
		<li>Hopeless Cycle no longer errors when undressing the prisoner after reloading or removing the sack early.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed transformation-maintaining accessories with sleep outfits</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Sleep outfits no longer remove accessories that maintain animal transformations, including honey hair clip, fish hairpin, carrot pin, and cat bell.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Combat encounters</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed many fights becoming stuck after choosing <strong>Give up</strong>, including Bailey, Eden, Kylar, Robin, Whitney, Gwylan, and Ivory Wraith encounters.</li>
		<li>Fixed enemy Arousal in swarm and struggle fights.</li>
		<li>Beast Arousal settings now work correctly.</li>
		<li>High Brawling scales correctly against multiple enemies.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed clothing systems</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Tattoos and body writing no longer show through clothes in affected front-facing image packs, like GooseFem.</li>
		<li>Clothing names, tags, and coverage no longer change incorrectly after loading.</li>
		<li>Chastity-belt variants are distinguished correctly.</li>
		<li>Chalet blackmail jobs now give and recognise the correct uniform.</li>
		<li>Sorting a wardrobe no longer deletes clothing.</li>
		<li>Earrings and rings can be removed while undressing in shops.</li>
		<li>Fixed held-item text, cursed outfits, shoe condition, damaged school skirts, and clothing colours.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Transformations and Mirror</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fangs, eyes, wings, and <strong>Mate for Life</strong> are no longer removed when another active transformation still provides them.</li>
		<li>Fixed Cat heterochromia, Bear pubic fur, and wing restoration.</li>
		<li>Mirror transformation options unlock at the correct stages.</li>
		<li>Added or fixed several transformation appearance toggles.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Identity and X-Change</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Short/Medium hair length is counted correctly.</li>
		<li>Pronoun rejection and Dysphoria behave consistently.</li>
		<li>Identity settings work more reliably on older saves.</li>
		<li>Fixed the <strong>Miniature</strong> body rejection option.</li>
		<li>Random X-Change pills given to NPCs now account for the NPC's body.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pregnancy records</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Great Hawk chicks only count as having left the nest after the player actually says farewell.</li>
		<li>Fixed a rare pregnancy record that could become permanently stuck.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed characters and events</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed Bailey-related time, money, Lust, inflation, and Ivory Wraith events in affected scenes/replays.</li>
		<li>Mod-added Love Interests no longer overwrite other character data.</li>
		<li>Minimaps now centre correctly on the player's position.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Updated Makeup and Hair Dye menu</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Makeup and hair dye settings are now combined into one <strong>Makeup and hair dye options</strong> menu in the mirror.</li>
		<li>Applying custom makeup no longer reloads the room or repeats room events.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Misc fixes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Missing weather or thermometer images no longer spam errors.</li>
		<li>Opening the game in another tab no longer prevents saving.</li>
		<li>Removed obsolete save-repair code and cleaned internal systems without affecting saves.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed named NPC gender settings</strong>
		<ul>
		<li><strong>Random Genders / Current Genders</strong> no longer resets individually selected named-NPC genders.</li>
		<li>Leaving the setting in the middle option preserves custom NPC gender choices.</li>
		<li><strong>All Male</strong> and <strong>All Female</strong> still override them.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Whitney Wild Night apology route</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Leaving Whitney during Wild Night now allows the existing apology/makeup route.</li>
		<li>Already affected saves work without a reset.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Title banner, pompoms, save loading, and performance fixes</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Simplified the title screen to use only the X-Change banner.</li>
		<li>Improved sidebar performance while moving between areas.</li>
		<li>Fixed pompoms disappearing while carrying a bag.</li>
		<li>Fixed the missing Aumasc pompom.</li>
		<li>Fixed missing image errors for several clothing items.</li>
		<li>Fixed some older compressed vanilla, DoLP, and DoLX saves failing to load.</li>
		<li>Fixed old saves getting stuck when loaded from removed scenes.</li>
		<li>Moving a vanilla save over while on Settings now returns the player to the previous location.</li>
		<li>Fixed Ear Slime chastity parasite equipping the wrong item.</li>
		<li>Removed an unused old banner setting from saves.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed pronouns</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Fixed pronoun issues in Kylar and Underground Brothel dialogue.</li>
		<li>Characters now use pronouns based on what they actually know about the player.</li>
		<li>Pronoun handling better follows current identity and preferences.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		<li><strong>Fixed Bailey's speech</strong>
		<ul>
		<li>Bailey no longer calls any large-chested or well-endowed player a cow.</li>
		<li>Cow-transformed characters retain the original cow-specific line.</li>
		<li>Other qualifying characters receive a more appropriate line.</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
		</ul>
